      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "Abstract Of what value is literature to the field of political science? I examine this question through a meditation on a new work of literary theory, Garl Saul Morson\u2019s Wonder Confronts Certainty: Russian Writers on the Timeless Questions and Why Their Answers Matter. Morson\u2019s theory of Russian literature as a source of wonder against the certainty found in Russian philosophy and politics has implications for debates in political science. My goal in this essay is to illustrate how literary analysis can be useful for political science as a source of both psychological and philosophical insight. Literature\u2019s emphasis on the specific and the individual tends to challenge more abstract social scientific frameworks, offering numerous opportunities for deeper reflection on the timeless questions in political science.",
